.TH IAD\-THEME.CONF 5 "2026-11-03" "iced-adaptive-design 0.1.0" "iced-adaptive-design Manual"
.SH NAME
theme.conf \- the theme files of an iad application and of the toolkit
.SH DESCRIPTION
The desktop configuration (\fBiad\-desktop.conf\fR(5)) is shared by every application. An application that needs its own look (its own colors, paddings and radii, tokens for objects only it has) uses theme files, in the same key\-file format.
.PP
Every setting is a \fItoken\fR: a typed value (a color \fI#rrggbb\fR or \fI#rrggbbaa\fR, a number, a bool or text) under a section and a key. A token only takes effect when it is set.
.SH FILES
Highest priority first:
.IP 1. 3
\fBHardcoded\fR in the application's code (\fBBuilder::hardcode\fR). Extremely discouraged: it cannot be changed without a rebuild, and every one is reported on stderr at startup.
.IP 2. 3
The application theme file, \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/<app\-id>/theme.conf\fR. The application declares its tokens and their defaults in a schema.
.IP 3. 3
The installed theme file: \fBIAD_THEME\fR=\fI<path>\fR (\fBnone\fR skips the external theme), else \fIdefault.conf\fR in \fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/iad/themes\fR, else in \fIiad/themes\fR of each \fI$XDG_DATA_DIRS\fR entry. The first file found is the only one read. A desktop or distribution installs its look there. The toolkit never writes it.
.IP 4. 3
The bundled base supplied by \fBBuilder::base_theme\fR or \fBConfig::load_with_base_theme\fR. Applications should bundle at least one theme file; \fIlibadwaita.conf\fR is recommended. An unset \fBIAD_THEME\fR or \fBIAD_THEME=none\fR never disables this explicit base. The selected external theme overlays it, with invalid values falling back to the base.
.PP
Below these, a token is its declared default. The toolkit has no built\-in look: without a bundled base or selected theme file it draws like HTML without CSS (black on white, square, thin grey rules, no shadows).
.PP
A missing application theme file is written from the declared defaults, every token commented out as \fI#key=default\fR under a description, so it documents the tokens and pins none of them. Uncomment a line to change it; delete the file to get a fresh one.
.SH TOKENS
.SS [colors], [light:colors] and [dark:colors]
\fBaccent\fR, \fBwindow\-bg\fR, \fBwindow\-fg\fR, \fBview\-bg\fR, \fBview\-fg\fR, \fBcard\-bg\fR, \fBcard\-fg\fR, \fBheaderbar\-bg\fR, \fBheaderbar\-fg\fR, \fBsidebar\-bg\fR, \fBsidebar\-fg\fR, \fBpopover\-bg\fR, \fBpopover\-fg\fR, \fBdialog\-bg\fR, \fBdialog\-fg\fR, \fBsuccess\fR, \fBwarning\fR, \fBdestructive\fR, \fBerror\fR. The variant section of the active scheme is read over \fB[colors]\fR. Companions: \fB\-fg\fR, \fB\-text\fR and \fB\-shade\fR keys.
.SS [metrics]
Numbers in px: \fBspace\-xs\fR to \fBspace\-xl\fR, \fBradius\-s\fR, \fBradius\-m\fR, \fBradius\-l\fR, \fBradius\-menu\fR, \fBradius\-popover\fR, \fBradius\-toast\fR, \fBradius\-window\fR, \fBbutton\-padding\-y\fR and \fB\-x\fR, \fBentry\-padding\-y\fR and \fB\-x\fR, \fBrow\-padding\-y\fR and \fB\-x\fR, \fBpage\-padding\-y\fR and \fB\-x\fR, \fBcard\-padding\fR, \fBdialog\-padding\fR, \fBpopover\-padding\fR, \fBbutton\-min\-height\fR, \fBentry\-min\-height\fR, \fBrow\-min\-height\fR, \fBborder\-width\fR, \fBicon\-size\fR, \fBgroup\-spacing\fR, \fBclamp\-maximum\fR, \fBheaderbar\-height\fR, \fBsidebar\-width\fR. Radii are not clamped to the HIG maxima.
.SS [typography]
\fBtext\-scale\fR multiplies every text size; \fBbase\-size\fR is the body size in px before the scale.
.SS [shadows]
\fBcard\fR, \fBpopover\fR, \fBdialog\fR, \fBosd\fR: CSS box\-shadow lists, e.g. \fI0 1px 3px 1px rgba(0, 0, 6, 0.07)\fR.
.SS [windows]
\fBbutton\-layout\fR (\fIstart:end\fR, e.g. \fI:minimize,maximize,close\fR), \fBbutton\-size\fR (px), \fBbutton\-radius\fR (percent of the size, 50% is a circle), \fBtitlebar\-double\-click\fR, \fBtitlebar\-middle\-click\fR and \fBtitlebar\-right\-click\fR (\fBtoggle\-maximize\fR, \fBmenu\fR, \fBminimize\fR, \fBlower\fR, \fBnone\fR).
.SS Other sections
Whatever the application declares for its own objects.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBiad\-desktop.conf\fR(5), \fBiad\fR(7)
